meta-middleware - CMake Hello World Layer
==========================================

This layer provides a simple CMake-based Hello World application example
for the Yocto Project.

Dependencies
============

This layer depends on:

  URI: git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky
  layers: meta
  branch: master

Contents
========

This layer contains:
  - recipes-example/hello-world: A simple CMake-based Hello World application

The hello-world recipe demonstrates:
  - How to create a CMake-based application in Yocto
  - Using the cmake class for building
  - Proper file installation to target image


Adding the meta-middleware layer to your build
===============================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-middleware'

Or manually add the layer to your bblayers.conf:

  BBLAYERS ?= " \
    /path/to/poky/meta \
    /path/to/poky/meta-poky \
    /path/to/poky/meta-yocto-bsp \
    /path/to/poky/meta-middleware \
    "

Building the Hello World Application
=====================================

To build the hello-world application:

  bitbake hello-world

To add it to your image, add to your local.conf or image recipe:

  IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " hello-world"

Then build your image:

  bitbake core-image-minimal

Testing
=======

After building and deploying the image, you can run:

  hello-world

Expected output:
  Hello, World from meta-middleware!
